1
00:00:00,552 --> 00:00:04,949
Tally helps businesses trade with unfamiliar suppliers using agreed evidence rules

2
00:00:04,959 --> 00:00:06,463
and verifiable records.

3
00:00:07,254 --> 00:00:11,053
Start in the app, then explore the public demo with paper deals.

4
00:00:15,544 --> 00:00:17,924
Open Companies and choose Highland Estates.

5
00:00:18,662 --> 00:00:21,639
Four milestones show three disputes and one lost dispute.

6
00:00:22,375 --> 00:00:25,233
Scroll to the completed trade and the delivery score.

7
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:27,465
These are paper records.

8
00:00:28,189 --> 00:00:32,787
The reliability score is provisional: its policy is a placeholder, not a calibrated

9
00:00:32,797 --> 00:00:33,578
credit rating.

10
00:00:35,541 --> 00:00:38,166
Next, ask Trust Check about the same supplier.

11
00:00:38,875 --> 00:00:41,189
Send company: highland-estates.

12
00:00:41,896 --> 00:00:44,753
The Coworker reads Tally's tools and explains the record.

13
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,912
This structured request needs no AI model.

14
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:50,611
It is a free, read-only preview.

15
00:00:51,307 --> 00:00:53,609
It makes no payment and saves no contract.

16
00:00:55,552 --> 00:00:58,487
In Deal Desk, choose the physical goods template.

17
00:00:59,303 --> 00:01:03,829
The coffee example is twelve hundred kilograms for four thousand test USDM. Agree

18
00:01:03,839 --> 00:01:07,264
the evidence rules, named inspector, and remedy before funding.

19
00:01:08,079 --> 00:01:09,828
Select Draft with the engine.

20
00:01:10,630 --> 00:01:15,163
The preview calculates payouts for each outcome, deadlines, and dispute windows.

21
00:01:15,978 --> 00:01:18,282
The sandbox sends no transaction.

22
00:01:20,552 --> 00:01:22,636
Now inspect a settled paper deal.

23
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:25,305
Both parties signed the terms.

24
00:01:26,094 --> 00:01:31,832
The agreed remedy lets the seller keep seventy percent: one thousand and fifty test USDM,
with

25
00:01:31,842 --> 00:01:34,132
four hundred and fifty refunded to the buyer.

26
00:01:34,947 --> 00:01:38,179
This settlement is paper; it sends no chain transaction.

27
00:01:40,551 --> 00:01:44,399
Payment verification uses a separate, real preproduction receipt.

28
00:01:45,212 --> 00:01:47,931
Load the Masumi example and run a fresh check.

29
00:01:48,742 --> 00:01:53,071
Beside it, an SSH terminal runs a separate Chainlink CRE command-line

30
00:01:53,081 --> 00:01:55,145
simulation for the same transaction.

31
00:01:55,957 --> 00:01:58,932
Watch the actual logs and successful completion.

32
00:01:59,743 --> 00:02:04,085
Both checks compare the recipient, the exact one test USDM received, and

33
00:02:04,095 --> 00:02:05,723
at least three confirmations.

34
00:02:06,534 --> 00:02:09,535
This is a single-node simulation reading Blockfrost.

35
00:02:10,346 --> 00:02:13,514
It has no oracle-network consensus or signature.

36
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:20,400
Finally, compare the same transaction hash and test USDM transfer in an independent

37
00:02:20,410 --> 00:02:22,353
Cardano preproduction explorer.

38
00:02:23,169 --> 00:02:27,625
Tally connects supplier assessment, agreed terms, and payment verification.
